.TH GETPGID 2 "2026-09-06" "EpinAnonymOS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
getpgid \- Linux syscall 121, as implemented by the EpinAnonymOS kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syscall(121, ...)
.br
kernel handler: \fBlinux_sys_getpgid\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Track A A4: setpgid records the task's process group for terminal ^C/^\ delivery.
getpgid/getpgrp keep the historical constant (1): busybox ash's job-control init
compares getpgrp() == tcgetpgrp(tty) to decide it owns the terminal, and both have
long reported 1, so the shell reaches its interactive prompt.  Returning real,
mismatched pgids here makes ash think it's a background shell and it never prompts.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION
Dispatched from \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/kernel_main.d\fR;
implemented in \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/syscalls/posix.d\fR.
.SH CAVEAT
This kernel emulates a SUBSET of the Linux ABI.  Behaviour that stock Linux
guarantees is not guaranteed here unless the DESCRIPTION says so.  Notably,
AF_UNIX reads return EAGAIN on an empty socket rather than blocking, and
absolute opens are resolved against the calling task's namespace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR anonymos-syscalls (7)
